+ * compact), `selected` is remapped to **compacted slot indices**, and the
+ * compacted set is moved once. Downstream kernels use selected[] purely as an
+ * index into the weight base and do not clamp it against 256, so the remapped
+ * slot indices can be fed straight in -- the same trick decode plays with
+ * `ident`.
